 /*
- * SWEET SE7 FIFO I2C / GT9896 Yellowstone / Focaltech 54:52 bring-up.
- * Call once after the scheduler is running; all work runs on one thread.
- * Requires ABL-loaded GENI I2C firmware; votes L11C through sweet_rpmh.c.
- * No firmware/config upload or direct PMIC writes. Only IC data write:
- * zero to GT9896's event status after reading a report. See touch2/report.md.
+ * CAT S62: Himax HX83112A (TDDI) touch on BLSP1 QUP1 I2C, polled.
+ *
+ * Stock dtbo (SDM 660 ... CEI): i2c_1 / himax,hxcommon @ 0x48, panel and
+ * display coords 1080x2160, IRQ TLMM gpio45 (active low), reset gpio25.
+ * The display (and with it the touch half of the TDDI) is brought up by
+ * ABL; this driver never powers rails and only releases the reset line if
+ * it is found driven low (boot-arg s62treset=1 forces a 20 ms pulse, which
+ * may disturb the panel).
+ *
+ * Bus: QUP v2.2.1 I2C mini-core in FIFO mode with V2 tags, polled; the
+ * sequence mirrors Linux i2c-qup.c qup_i2c_xfer_v2 (write msg, PAUSE,
+ * read msg). Clocks: GCC BLSP1 AHB vote and BLSP1_QUP1_I2C_APPS from XO.
+ * Events: hx83112b format (Linux himax_hx83112b.c) - 56 bytes from 0x30:
+ * 10 x {be16 x, be16 y}, 10 majors, 2 pad, point count, 2 pad, checksum
+ * (byte sum == 0 mod 256). x/y == 0xffff marks an empty slot.
  */
